  "evidence": [
    "Standing user permission: genuine source C++, act on cross-owner structural evidence, preserve original bugs and all historical identities/spans/claims, coordinator-reviewed manual integration. This scope unifies both current owners; it does not assert their original historical TU.",
    "Pinned original four DesignWin picker normal epilogues expand the same six close-state stores and thirteen cleanup calls as SelectPartWin destruction. Current separate-TU source hides that body. Finite immutable actual-recipe overlays at base 2c2c407fba69ba73e4556995d5cc2cf85e3e0308 show both ordinary shared-TU and header visibility restore all four twelve-state EH predecessor graphs. Header-visible close loses standalone original0x432970; ordinary shared-TU retains all89 mapped identities and all46 locally exact bodies. Remaining caller frame-transfer/instruction differences are explicit obligations, not accepted exactness.",
    "Authorize move of unchanged SelectPartWin methods and complete mapping/binding/history bytes into designwin.cpp before its existing callers; retain selectpartwin.h and real hierarchy, members, cleanup semantics, signatures and source-owned providers. Remove obsolete selectpartwin.cpp and exactly its two CMake entries. No product include-CPP, manual cleanup, padding, flags/exports/forced-inline, guessed types, new wrappers or original-marker edits. No claim demotion or baseline reset.",
    "Adapt existing actual-source test paths and compile-profile expectations to the new emitting TU without deleting assertions, changing expected effects or weakening mutants. Add focused structural continuity checks if useful. Coordinator owns source transfer, native writes, Git, compiler leasing/preparation/build/link and manual merge; cheaper worker may only edit listed tests in the isolated checkout. Preserve failed trials and discoveries privately; no fresh repetitions of the three completed unchanged-context candidates.",
    "Private evidence: .opensmacx/recovery/parallel-match-oct22w/selectpart-native-probe/report.json (10 controlled compiler calls), selectpart-shared-tu-probe/report.json (3 calls, unchanged replica plus damaged genuine destructor), selectpart-original-close-review.md and selectpart-frame-transfer-review.md. Controls and mapped local exactness do not prove relocation targets, linked provider selection, outside-scope residual, runtime or game acceptance. Require independent physical/source review and fresh whole build/link, mapping/claim/reference/source checks and mapped census before integration."
  ],
